## Proposed Changes

### 1. Database Schema (Laravel)

We only need three clean tables to manage this workflow:

#### `courses` (To manage what courses are displayed and their prices)
*   `id` (BIGINT, PK, Auto Increment)
*   `title` (VARCHAR)
*   `slug` (VARCHAR, Unique)
*   `description` (TEXT)
*   `price` (DECIMAL 10,2)
*   `whatsapp_group_link` (VARCHAR) - The invite link users receive after payment.
*   `is_active` (BOOLEAN, Default: true)
*   `timestamps`

#### `course_registrations` (To store student details)
*   `id` (BIGINT, PK, Auto Increment)
*   `course_id` (FOREIGN KEY -> `courses.id`)
*   `name` (VARCHAR)
*   `email` (VARCHAR)
*   `whatsapp_number` (VARCHAR)
*   `company_name` (VARCHAR, Nullable)
*   `status` (ENUM: 'pending', 'completed')
*   `timestamps`

#### `transactions` (To track Xendit payments)
*   `id` (BIGINT, PK, Auto Increment)
*   `registration_id` (FOREIGN KEY -> `course_registrations.id`, Cascade on delete)
*   `invoice_number` (VARCHAR, Unique)
*   `amount` (DECIMAL 10,2)
*   `status` (ENUM: 'pending', 'paid', 'expired', 'failed')
*   `xendit_invoice_id` (VARCHAR, Nullable)
*   `payment_url` (VARCHAR, Nullable)
*   `paid_at` (TIMESTAMP, Nullable)
*   `timestamps`

---

### 2. Backend API Endpoint Details

#### Public Course Catalog
*   `GET /api/courses` - Fetch courses for listing.
*   `GET /api/courses/{slug}` - Fetch specific course.

#### Checkout & Payments
*   `POST /api/course-registrations` - Creates registration and transaction, calls Xendit Invoice, and returns `payment_url`.
*   `GET /api/transactions/status/{invoice_number}` - Returns transaction status and the `whatsapp_group_link` if status is `'paid'`.
*   `POST /api/webhooks/xendit` - Public callback endpoint that updates status and marks registration as `'completed'`.

#### Admin CMS (Existing Sanctum Auth)
*   `GET/POST/PUT/DELETE /api/courses` - Admin management of courses.
*   `GET /api/admin/registrations` - List registrations (leads) showing name, WA, course, and payment status so PIC personnel can track.

---

### 3. Frontend Next.js Pages

#### Course Section
*   `/courses` - Course selection grid.
*   `/courses/[slug]` - Course info with a "Daftar & Bayar" form.
*   `/checkout/pending` - Page shown if redirect happens before webhook completes.
*   `/checkout/success?invoice_number=INV-xxx` - Polling page that checks payment status; displays the **WhatsApp Group Invite Button** when payment is confirmed.

